[
    {
        "content": "<p>Suppose I have the following variables </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mon</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BraidedCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GrpObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsCommMonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EndRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I did not see any code in <code>Mathlib</code> which gives <code>EndRing A</code> a ring structure. Does there exist something along these lines in Mathlib (i.e., a ring of endomorphisms for group objects)?</p>",
        "id": 621531265,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788472037
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>shows that even the monoid structure is missing.</p>",
        "id": 621612712,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1788503389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I tried this and </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>as well, and got an error. I was just hoping that maybe there is some other definition somewhere in <code>Mathlib</code> which has the required instances. I'm guessing the answer is no, then! <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 621647764,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788512969
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably not (-;</p>",
        "id": 621648832,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1788513219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"112680\">Johan Commelin</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621612712\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>shows that even the monoid structure is missing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>have you tried looking in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.End#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.End</a></p>",
