    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span> I did see this file yesterday. But, as far as I understood it deals with endfunctors of categories, rather an endomorphisms of Abelian group objects.</p>",
        "id": 621670166,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788518995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it looks like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Preadditive.instRingEnd#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Preadditive.instRingEnd</a> is the ring structure in a preadditive category (though I don't think you get a preadditive structure on <code>Mon</code> since you could have noncommutative monoid objects?)</p>",
        "id": 621671490,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788519378
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(could that be solved by working in <code>Mon (Mon C)</code> or something?)</p>",
        "id": 621671876,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788519508
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh, there's a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.CommGrp#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.CommGrp</a> as well, perhaps that could work</p>",
        "id": 621672105,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788519580
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Cartesian/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.Hom.addCommGroup\">CategoryTheory.Hom.addCommGroup</a></p>",
        "id": 621680242,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788521965
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Cartesian/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.Hom.commGroup\">CategoryTheory.Hom.commGroup</a> (no <code>to_additive</code>?)<br>\nso <code>#synth Monoid (Hom (mk A) (mk A))</code> should work if you remove the <code>mk</code>?</p>\n<p>Separately we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Endomorphism.html#CategoryTheory.End.monoid\">CategoryTheory.End.monoid</a>, and we'll need distributivity</p>",
        "id": 621680802,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788522125
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"759692\">@Abhijit A J</span> One thing to be aware of is that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GrpObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsCommMonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is geared towards multiplicative notation, instead of additive notation.</p>",
        "id": 621682661,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1788522715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621672105\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>oh, there's a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.CommGrp#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.CommGrp</a> as well, perhaps that could work</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Unfortunately, <code>CommGrp C</code> does not have an <code>Preadditive</code> instance. So, I cannot use the ring structure from there.</p>",
        "id": 621685164,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788523441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621680802\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Cartesian/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.Hom.commGroup\">CategoryTheory.Hom.commGroup</a> (no <code>to_additive</code>?)<br>\nso <code>#synth Monoid (Hom (mk A) (mk A))</code> should work if you remove the <code>mk</code>?</p>\n<p>Separately we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Endomorphism.html#CategoryTheory.End.monoid\">CategoryTheory.End.monoid</a>, and we'll need distributivity</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>These are unfortunately all the endomorphisms of the the object. I only want to consider the endomorphisms that preserve the group structure.</p>",
        "id": 621685657,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788523569
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Which is why I don't want to remove the <code>mk</code></p>",
        "id": 621685782,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788523599
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"759692\">Abhijit A J</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621685657\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>These are unfortunately all the endomorphisms of the the object. I only want to consider the endomorphisms that preserve the group structure.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Surely the morphisms in the category of (commutative) group objects are precisely the group homomorphisms?</p>",
        "id": 621686497,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788523793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"112680\">Johan Commelin</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621682661\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"759692\">Abhijit A J</span> One thing to be aware of is that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GrpObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsCommMonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is geared towards multiplicative notation, instead of additive notation.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, I thought that that might be the problem. But, it does not seem to have any binary operation defined on it.<br>\nAs we discussed in another chat yesterday, I am working on CM Abelian varieties. And, before I can even define CM structures, I need to define the Endomorphism ring of an abelian variety - which is defined using <code>[GroupObj A]</code> in mathlib. So, I was hoping that that was already defined somewhere in Mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 621686821,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788523868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>perhaps we want a <code>CategoryTheory.AddCommGrp</code>?</p>",
        "id": 621687000,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788523921
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621686497\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Surely the morphisms in the category of (commutative) group objects are precisely the group homomorphisms?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, but to use the ring structure you mentioned above, I need this to not give an error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">CommGrp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Which it unfortunately does</p>",
        "id": 621687461,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788524045
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621687000\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>perhaps we want a <code>CategoryTheory.AddCommGrp</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That would be nice!</p>",
        "id": 621687817,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788524135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I hope I haven't made any mistakes when checking all your suggestions! Please let me know if I said some silly! <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 621688100,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788524217
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>These are unfortunately all the endomorphisms of the the object. I only want to consider the endomorphisms that preserve the group structure.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So you want a categorical version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Hom/Instances.html#MonoidHom.instCommMonoid\">MonoidHom.instCommMonoid</a></p>\n<p>I think you can put a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Preadditive/Basic.html#CategoryTheory.Preadditive\">CategoryTheory.Preadditive</a> structure on \"CategoryTheory.AddCommGrp\" and use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Preadditive.instRingEnd#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Preadditive.instRingEnd</a>.<br>\nThere's currently <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.AddGrp\">AddGrp</a> as well as CommGrp (use in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Preadditive/CommGrp_.html#CategoryTheory.Preadditive.commGrpEquivalence\">CategoryTheory.Preadditive.commGrpEquivalence</a> which mixes additive and multiplicative!) but not AddCommGrp.</p>",
        "id": 621691371,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788524685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621691371\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So you want a categorical version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Hom/Instances.html#MonoidHom.instCommMonoid\">MonoidHom.instCommMonoid</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I thought we wanted a categorical version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=AddMonoid.End.instRing#doc\">docs#AddMonoid.End.instRing</a></p>",
        "id": 621691936,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788524769
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, intermediate goal vs eventual goal</p>",
        "id": 621693221,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788524968
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621691936\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621691371\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So you want a categorical version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Hom/Instances.html#MonoidHom.instCommMonoid\">MonoidHom.instCommMonoid</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I thought we wanted a categorical version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=AddMonoid.End.instRing#doc\">docs#AddMonoid.End.instRing</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yup, I want the ring structure. Currently, I am considering just doing it by hand. i.e.,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BraidedCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsCommMonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But, if there are better suggestions, I am open to it.</p>",
        "id": 621693408,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788524999
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"224323\">@Junyan Xu</span> I haven't tried that. But, do you think it would easier/ better than defining the addition directly?</p>",
        "id": 621693775,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788525052
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know, defining directly could be more flexible: unlike MonoidHom which works for Monoid, Group and CommGroup simultaneously, morphisms in different categories are not defeq, so it might be advantageous to stick with the most general category, i.e. <code>Mon</code>/<code>AddMon</code>.</p>",
        "id": 621706047,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788527142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you want <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.AddGrpObj\">CategoryTheory.AddGrpObj</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Mon.html#CategoryTheory.IsCommAddMonObj\">CategoryTheory.IsCommAddMonObj</a><br>\n(with MonObj you only get Semiring)</p>",
        "id": 621709680,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1788528009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, thanks. I'll define it directly, then.</p>",
        "id": 621716378,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788529580
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/621709680\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think you want <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Grp.html#CategoryTheory.AddGrpObj\">CategoryTheory.AddGrpObj</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Mon.html#CategoryTheory.IsCommAddMonObj\">CategoryTheory.IsCommAddMonObj</a><br>\n(with MonObj you only get Semiring)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, that's true. I thought I'd define the semiring structure when it  is a monoid object. Then, when it is a group object, the ring structure.</p>",
        "id": 621716631,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788529642
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have been able to define the <code>Ring</code> instance for the endomorphims ring for an abelian group object. I first defined a <code>Semiring</code>instance for a monoidal object, and an <code>AddCommGroup</code> for a group object.<br>\nI am guessing that this might be useful to someone else as well, so I was wondering if it should be added to <code>Mathlib</code>. I'd like to know others' thoughts.</p>",
        "id": 622124282,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788728526
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, please open a PR so we can look at your code!<br>\nAlthough if it is quite long (e.g. several hundred lines) you may want to consider splitting it up to make the  review more manageable.</p>",
        "id": 622139441,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788738324
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is the first time I'm contributing to mathlib. So, this question might be dumb.<br>\nI broke the file into three small ones (because it was roughly 370 line of code). I have submitted a PR for the first part.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Do I have to do anything now? Like, do I just wait, or do I need to drop a message in some channel here?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Should I wait until my first PR is merged to submit the second (the second depends on the first).</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 622316183,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788796085
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"759692\">Abhijit A J</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/622316183\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do I have to do anything now?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It will automatically get added to the review queue, then someone will review it. You will know if action is needed from you if they add the <code>awaiting-author</code> tag on github. </p>\n<p>However, I'd also encourage you to drop a link in this thread, so that people here can easily find/review it. You can automatically generate links to Mathlib PRs hashtag, e.g. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/12345\">#12345</a></p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"759692\">Abhijit A J</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Ring.20structure.20on.20the.20Endomorphism/near/622316183\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Should I wait until my first PR is merged to submit the second</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You're welcome to open the second one now, but you should indicate the dependency in the PR description. For example, notice how <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42528\">#42528</a> includes </p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>[ ] depends on: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43524\">#43524</a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This way, it gets automatically tagged as <code>blocked-by-other-PR</code> and then we won't review it until the first one is merged.</p>",
        "id": 622334135,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788800049
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perfect. This is a very detailed answer. Thank you very much <span aria-label=\"smiling face\" class=\"emoji emoji-263a\" role=\"img\" title=\"smiling face\">:smiling_face:</span></p>",
